    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sōtădes</span></b> , is,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σωτάδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an obscene Greek
			poet</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 2, 86, 2</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sō-tădēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>in the manner of Sotades</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 90</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 9, 4, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 8, 6</span></i>; Ter. Maur.
			pp. 2415 and 2446 P.; <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 14,
			29</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sōtădĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Sotadic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 5, 3, 2</span></i>
			. —<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: L. Attius in Sotadicorum libro, <i>Sotadic
				verses</i>, Geli. 7, 9, 16.</div>
